@* MultiSelect's Overview, written by hand after Combobox's, whose script it shares: choosing
   several (previewed in each mode), at least one with ids for values, enum options with icons,
   sizes and states, and its own words. Accessibility and See also come from the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>For a short list, a <Anchor Href="docs/components/checkbox-group">CheckboxGroup</Anchor> shows every option at once; for one choice, use a <Anchor Href="docs/components/combobox">Combobox</Anchor> or a <Anchor Href="docs/components/select">Select</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Choosing several</Heading>
<TextBlock>Bind <Code>@@bind-Value</Code> to a collection and pass the options to <Code>Items</Code>: chosen options show as chips, typing filters the list, ignoring case and accents, and the list stays open as people choose.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="multi-select-chips" />
<TextBlock>The collection can be an array, a <Code>List&lt;T&gt;</Code>, a <Code>HashSet&lt;T&gt;</Code> or an interface they implement. Each choice posts as a repeated form field, and an empty choice posts nothing: on a static page the property is then null, or the model isn't bound at all, so set defaults only when the request isn't a post, as the example does (<Anchor Href="docs/troubleshooting/empty-selection">why</Anchor>). <Code>[MaxLength]</Code> limits how many, checked on the server.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">At least one, with a placeholder</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>[Required]</Code> and <Code>[MinLength(1)]</Code> together to need at least one choice, and <Code>ItemText</Code> to name options whose values are ids.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="multi-select-reviewers" />
<TextBlock>The browser checks <Code>[Required]</Code> before posting. On the server, <Code>[Required]</Code> catches an empty choice on a static page, where the property is null, and <Code>[MinLength(1)]</Code> catches it on an interactive page, where it's an empty list. A post can carry values that aren't among the options, and they reach the model, so check them on the server, as the example does.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Enum options with icons</Heading>
<TextBlock>For an enum, pass its values to <Code>Items</Code> (<Code>Enum.GetValues&lt;IssueLabel&gt;()</Code>), and use <Code>ItemTemplate</Code> to add markup to each option, such as an icon; chips show <Code>ItemText</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="multi-select-enum-icons" />
<TextBlock>Options are named by the enum's <Code>[Display(Name)]</Code> when it has one.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Sizes, read-only and disabled</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Size</Code> to line up with buttons and other fields, <Code>ReadOnly</Code> for choices that post but can't change, and <Code>Disabled</Code> for ones that don't post.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="multi-select-states" />
<TextBlock>HTML has no read-only select, so a read-only MultiSelect shows its choices in a read-only text field and posts them from hidden inputs.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Its own words</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>EmptyText</Code> for "No matches", <Code>ToggleLabel</Code> for the name of the button that opens the list and <Code>RemoveLabel</Code> for the start of each chip's remove button name ("Remove Blazor"), or set them for the whole app as in <Anchor Href="docs/common/text">Text and other languages</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        @* Strings: each is its own text. *@
        <MultiSelect @bind-Value="Model!.Skills" Items="AllSkills" Placeholder="Add skills" />

        @* Ids, named for people. *@
        <MultiSelect @bind-Value="Model!.ReviewerIds" Items="People.Keys"
                     ItemText="id => People.GetValueOrDefault(id, id.ToString())" />

        @* An enum's values. *@
        <MultiSelect @bind-Value="Model!.Days" Items="Enum.GetValues<DayOfWeek>()" />
        """;
}
